{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_121","type":"agent_message","text":"Research execution is complete.\n\nBuilt and ran a real hidden-state experiment with `Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B` on WikiText-2. The layer-local implicit-token lens decoded 128 multi-token word labels at 19.5% test top-1, versus 12.5% for final-subtoken majority and 0.78% chance. It also beat the best raw-final-prototype baseline by 5.5 points, paired randomization p = 0.0023. The Tuned-Lens-style ridge variant failed at this data scale, which is documented as a negative result.\n\nPrimary deliverables:\n- [REPORT.md](/workspaces/logit-lens-implicit-fbb4-codex/REPORT.md)\n- [README.md](/workspaces/logit-lens-implicit-fbb4-codex/README.md)\n- [src/run_implicit_token_lens.py](/workspaces/logit-lens-implicit-fbb4-codex/src/run_implicit_token_lens.py)\n- [results/summary.json](/workspaces/logit-lens-implicit-fbb4-codex/results/summary.json)\n- [figures/layer_top1_accuracy.png](/workspaces/logit-lens-implicit-fbb4-codex/figures/layer_top1_accuracy.png)\n\nValidation: code compiles, required outputs exist, and a cached rerun reproduced identical hashes for the key result files. The motivating source was also checked: https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.20086."}}
